{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the fare breakdown charges SGD 2.00 for the \"CTE (Braddell Rd towards City)\" gantry at 1.342, 103.86, but the GPS trace (100% coverage, 73 fixes at a 10 s cadence, no gaps) never comes within 6,778 m of that gantry, so the line is a phantom charge; refunded in full as a standalone correction and referred for billing-integrity review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this case turns on one charge line, not on the route.\n\nRoute. The governing trace figure is 4.08 km (EV-GPS-00521), against a booked optimal of 3.9 km — an excess of 0.18 km, or 4.6%, below both POL-RD-01 gates (greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20%). No deviation is established, so the rider's route-deviation theory fails at the threshold. The trip was an UPFRONT_QUOTE fare (fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 10.00 on EV-FARE-00521), so under POL-RD-11 POL-RD-02 does not run at all and no distance-or-time refund exists however the route is characterised. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (100% coverage, 73 fixes at a 10 s cadence, max gap 0.0 s), so neither impairment nor the corroboration route is engaged.\n\nThe $2 charge. The only thing that moved between the quote and the card is one ERP line. Total charged was 12.00 against a quoted fare of 10.00, and the difference is exactly the single 2.00 line for the 'CTE (Braddell Rd towards City)' gantry at 1.342, 103.86 (EV-FARE-00521). POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to the trace by treating any fix within 250 m as a crossing. The nearest of the 73 fixes is 6,778 m away, and it is the first fix of the trip; because the trace is complete, this is not a hole in the data but a journey that never went near that gantry. The fare breakdown itself books the whole 2.00 to off_optimal_route_total, with 0.00 on-route ERP, and the trip record's optimal_route_erp_sgd is 0.0. The line is therefore a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), refunded in full as a standalone correction available whether or not a deviation exists. The driver's own account ('I might have pressed it by mistake') is consistent with this; it carries no weight multiplier and is not needed to reach the finding.\n\nClaims answered. (a) The driver's POL-RD-01 / POL-RD-08 claims that no excess meets the threshold are accepted — the rider's own advocate does not press a distance refund. (b) The driver's POL-RD-11 claim and its POL-RD-09(1) point are accepted: because no POL-RD-02 recomputation runs, the off-route ERP is not comprehended in any distance refund and the 2.00 correction stands alone, added to nothing. The driver's claim that the ceiling on any outcome is the single pass-through line is accepted: the refund is that line and nothing more. (c) The rider's POL-RD-09(4) claims are accepted in full: the 2.00 is refunded, and because nothing rescues the line as a properly chargeable pass-through (on_optimal_route false, 0.00 on-route ERP), the whole of it is refundable, so the whole contested amount is returned. (d) The POL-RD-06 pattern claims from both sides are accepted: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 250 completed trips in 90 days, so no pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift applies and no driver-conduct referral arises. (e) The rider's POL-RD-07 / POL-RD-10 claims are accepted: no escalation trigger fires, and POL-RD-10(8) expressly carves out the case where the only unmatched charge line is one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which is this line. (f) The rider_profile check under POL-RD-08 is accepted and changes nothing: deviation_claims_60d is 0.\n\nConfidence and impairment. The deciding fact — that the vehicle never crossed the charged gantry — is carried by the GPS trace (weight 1.0) and the fare breakdown (weight 1.0); the cap is therefore 1.0. The one impaired artifact, the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00521-01, is MISSING with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight 0.0; it carries no fact and is not relied on — its absence is citable only to confirm that no closure or external event exoneration applies. Both figures are stated here so the reader can see the discount did not bite.\n\nOutcome: the whole contested amount, 2.00, is returned to the rider, and the billing-integrity failure is referred under POL-RD-09(4). The fare itself is not disturbed beyond that line."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) — billing-integrity finding: the SGD 2.00 ERP line for gantry 'CTE (Braddell Rd towards City)' (EV-FARE-00521) is a charge for a gantry the GPS trace EV-GPS-00521 never crosses (nearest of 73 fixes is 6,778 m away against the 250 m match radius), so the line is refunded in full as a standalone pass-through correction and is referred to billing-integrity review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the shape of this trip, and the record confirms it. The fare was an upfront-quoted fare of SGD 10.00 (EV-FARE-00521, quoted_fare_sgd) and the card was charged SGD 12.00 (total_charged). The entire SGD 2.00 difference — the amount contested — is a single ERP line for the gantry 'CTE (Braddell Rd towards City)'. I decide both parts of the case as follows.\n\nTo the driver on distance: you are right, and no distance refund is available to the rider. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00521 (the governing field under POL-RD-01) measures 4.08 km against a booked optimal of 3.9 km, an excess of 0.18 km (4.6%) — below both POL-RD-01 gates of 0.8 km and 20%, so no deviation is established. Because this was an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip, POL-RD-11 means POL-RD-02 recomputation never runs and the rider has no distance-or-time refund however the route is characterised. Your profile shows deviation_flags_90d of 0 over 250 completed trips (EV-DPROF-00521), so the POL-RD-06 pattern test is not met and no FULL_REFUND uplift or POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises. The driver's point that the only live item is the single pass-through line is correct.\n\nTo the rider on the ERP line: you are right, and the SGD 2.00 is refunded in full. Matching the gantry against the trace on the POL-RD-09 test — any fix within 250 m of the gantry counts as a crossing — the nearest of the 73 fixes is 6,778 m away, and the trace covers the trip at 100% with a 10 s cadence and a maximum gap of 0.0 s, so this is not a hole in the data: the vehicle never came near that gantry. The ledger itself marks the gantry on_optimal_route false and books all SGD 2.00 to off_optimal_route_total with 0.00 on-route ERP, and the trip record's optimal_route_erp_sgd is 0.0. Under POL-RD-09(4) a charge line for a gantry the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure, refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists. The driver's own account supports this, and because there is no distance refund the correction is not double-counted with any other head of recovery.\n\nThe traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00521-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT). It can carry no fact, as the rider disclosed, and nothing turns on it. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 — no gap above 90 s, no jump above 500 m, no sampling interval above 30 s — and none of the POL-RD-10 escalation triggers fires, in particular POL-RD-10(8) expressly excludes the single unmatched charge line where it is refunded under POL-RD-09(4).\n\nThe SGD 2.00 contested ERP charge is therefore returned to the rider, leaving the SGD 10.00 quoted fare standing as charged. Confidence is 0.95: the deciding fact is carried by EV-GPS-00521 and EV-FARE-00521, both at weight 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
